# Reverse-proxies the Loreline UI/API onto standard ports for the
# docker-compose stack. WebSocket upgrades (/ws/transcript, /ws/logs,
# /ws/audio/level) are proxied automatically - reverse_proxy needs no special
# config for them.
#
# :443 terminates TLS so the LAN login password isn't sent in the clear (the
# app itself only ever sees plain HTTP from Caddy). `tls internal` self-signs
# against Caddy's own local CA: browsers will show a "not trusted" warning
# until a device explicitly trusts that CA (see Caddy's docs on its local
# CA for how to export/install it). If this box has a real domain with
# public DNS, replace both addresses below with that hostname and drop
# `tls internal` - Caddy then gets a real Let's Encrypt certificate
# automatically instead.
#
# :80 stays available with no redirect, so a device that hasn't trusted the
# internal CA yet isn't locked out of the app entirely.
#
# `tls internal` needs a hostname to mint a certificate for. There isn't a
# fixed one here - this box is reached by whatever LAN IP it happens to have
# - so `on_demand` tells Caddy to issue a cert for whatever name/IP a client
# actually connects with, the first time it connects. No `ask` allowlist /
# rate limiting configured: anything reaching this box is already inside the
# LAN, unlike a public-facing on-demand-TLS site where an `ask` endpoint
# guards against strangers flooding cert issuance for junk hostnames.

:443 {
	tls internal {
		on_demand
	}
	reverse_proxy app:8000
}

:80 {
	reverse_proxy app:8000
}
